.\"
.\" FORK(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH FORK 2 "January 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
fork \- create a child process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.B pid_t fork(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR fork ()
creates a new process by duplicating the calling process. The new process
is referred to as the
.I child
process. The calling process is referred to as the
.I parent
process.
.PP
The child process is an exact duplicate of the parent process except for:
.IP \(bu 3
The child has a unique process ID.
.IP \(bu 3
The child's parent process ID is the process ID of the parent.
.IP \(bu 3
The child does not inherit pending signals.
.IP \(bu 3
File locks are not inherited.
.PP
Substrate implements Copy-on-Write (COW) for memory pages, so fork is
efficient even for large processes.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, the PID of the child process is returned in the parent,
and 0 is returned in the child.
.PP
On failure, \-1 is returned in the parent, no child process is created,
and
.I errno
is set appropriately.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EAGAIN
Cannot allocate sufficient memory or process table entry.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
Failed to allocate memory for child process.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 2 (SYS_FORK)
Arguments:      none

    push $0
    mov eax, 2
    int $0x80
.fi
.SS Copy-on-Write
Substrate uses pmap-level COW. When a page is written after fork,
a page fault triggers duplication. Use
.BR pmap_stats (2)
to query COW statistics.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vfork (2),
.BR clone (2),
.BR execve (2),
.BR wait (2),
.BR pmap_stats (2),
.BR substrate (7)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2001, POSIX.1-2008.
